<article class="env-lemma" id="05QP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05QP">Lemma <span data-tag="05QP">13.4.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a pre-triangulated category. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (0, b, 0), (0, b', 0) : (X, Y, Z, f, g, h) \to (X, Y, Z, f, g, h)  \]
</div>
  <p> be endomorphisms of a distinguished triangle. Then $bb' = 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Picture 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[r] \ar[d]^0 &  Y \ar[r] \ar[d]^{b, b'} \ar@{..>}[ld]^\alpha &  Z \ar[r] \ar[d]^0 \ar@{..>}[ld]^\beta &  X[1] \ar[d]^0 \\  X \ar[r] &  Y \ar[r] &  Z \ar[r] &  X[1] }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Applying Lemma <a href="/tag/0149" data-tag="0149">13.4.2</a> we find dotted arrows $\alpha $ and $\beta $ such that $b' = f \circ \alpha $ and $b = \beta \circ g$. Then $bb' = \beta \circ g \circ f \circ \alpha = 0$ as $g \circ f = 0$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0146" data-tag="0146">13.4.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>